From e75637f1c2ddaf64dee760a400e9aa82dc81350b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fabio <fabio@git.it>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:24:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] serve webdav: stop deep listings and cut off uploads hurting
 small hosts (backport)

A PROPFIND with Depth: infinity, or with no Depth header, lists the
whole tree in one response. On a big tree this reads every directory
into the directory cache, using memory in proportion to the number of
files, which can run a small host out of memory.

With --disable-depth-infinity these requests are rejected with 403 and
a propfind-finite-depth error, as allowed by RFC 4918, and clients list
one level at a time with Depth: 1. The default is unchanged.

When the body of a PUT was cut off part way, for example because the
client was killed mid-stream, the webdav handler closed the file
normally and the part received was stored as if it were the whole
file. The write is now abandoned instead, so the upload fails and the
partial file is discarded.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 cmd/serve/webdav/webdav.go      | 71 +++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 cmd/serve/webdav/webdav_test.go | 82 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 147 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

